1
00:00:01,209 --> 00:00:02,252
Morning.

2
00:00:02,252 --> 00:00:03,337
Hi.

3
00:00:03,337 --> 00:00:05,213
Oh, how was your
date last night?

4
00:00:05,213 --> 00:00:06,548
Pretty good.

5
00:00:06,548 --> 00:00:08,049
Oh, good.

6
00:00:10,010 --> 00:00:11,178
( screams )

7
00:00:11,178 --> 00:00:12,346
Oh, my God. Sorry.

8
00:00:13,597 --> 00:00:15,098
Okay. Really good.

9
00:00:15,098 --> 00:00:17,476
Anyway, I've got to go.
I'm late for work.

10
00:00:17,476 --> 00:00:19,728
You're going to leave
this person with me?

11
00:00:19,728 --> 00:00:21,522
Hey, don't worry.
She's a terrific girl.

12
00:00:21,522 --> 00:00:23,315
And hey, listen.

13
00:00:23,315 --> 00:00:25,526
You do me a favor?
When she comes out,
could you just mention

14
00:00:25,526 --> 00:00:28,362
that I'm not looking for
a serious relationship?
That'd be great.

15
00:00:28,362 --> 00:00:30,447
Whoa! What, are you kidding?

16
00:00:30,447 --> 00:00:32,825
Just casually slip
it in, you know?

17
00:00:32,825 --> 00:00:34,242
Lay the groundwork.

18
00:00:34,242 --> 00:00:36,871
Tell her... I'm a loner.
No, an outlaw.

19
00:00:36,871 --> 00:00:40,833
She doesn't want to
get mixed up with
the likes of me.

20
00:00:40,833 --> 00:00:42,751
You know what, that's
a lot to remember.

21
00:00:42,751 --> 00:00:44,753
Can't I just tell her
that you're a pig?

22
00:00:44,753 --> 00:00:47,088
Hey, I'm going to
call her later myself.

23
00:00:47,088 --> 00:00:48,423
Honest.

24
00:00:48,423 --> 00:00:50,425
Look, come on, Chandler
used to do it.

25
00:00:50,425 --> 00:00:52,720
He'd even make
the girl pancakes.

26
00:00:52,720 --> 00:00:55,597
Plus he'd make extras
and leave them for me.

27
00:00:55,597 --> 00:00:57,975
Well, forget it, I'm not telling
that girl anything.

28
00:00:57,975 --> 00:00:59,184
That is not my responsibility.

29
00:00:59,184 --> 00:01:00,519
Fine.

30
00:01:00,519 --> 00:01:03,355
Now, where did we land
on those pancakes?

31
00:01:03,355 --> 00:01:04,481
Get out.

32
00:01:08,027 --> 00:01:09,528
Hi.
Hi.

33
00:01:09,528 --> 00:01:11,112
Sorry about that

34
00:01:11,112 --> 00:01:12,907
but I couldn't get that lock
to work on the door.

35
00:01:12,907 --> 00:01:16,201
Yeah, Joey kind of disabled it
when I moved in.

36
00:01:16,201 --> 00:01:18,037
You must be Rachel, I'm Erin.

37
00:01:18,037 --> 00:01:19,621
Hi.
Hi.

38
00:01:19,621 --> 00:01:22,165
I don't mean this to sound
like high school

39
00:01:22,165 --> 00:01:24,209
but did he say
anything about me?

40
00:01:27,128 --> 00:01:29,172
Would you like
some pancakes?

41
00:01:29,172 --> 00:01:30,716
Yeah.

42
00:01:35,596 --> 00:01:40,768
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

43
00:01:40,768 --> 00:01:43,478
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

44
00:01:43,478 --> 00:01:45,355
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

45
00:01:45,355 --> 00:01:50,151
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

46
00:01:50,151 --> 00:01:53,447
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

47
00:01:53,447 --> 00:01:55,741
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

48
00:01:55,741 --> 00:01:59,036
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

49
00:01:59,036 --> 00:02:02,748
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

50
00:02:10,965 --> 00:02:13,174
Come on, why
are we here?

51
00:02:13,174 --> 00:02:16,095
Okay, okay,
take a guess.

52
00:02:16,095 --> 00:02:17,972
The hot chicks.

53
00:02:17,972 --> 00:02:21,642
Okay, okay, I was
typing names into
the library computer

54
00:02:21,642 --> 00:02:24,103
earlier, you know,
you know, for fun...

55
00:02:24,103 --> 00:02:28,231
and I typed mine
in and, uh, guess
what came up?

56
00:02:28,231 --> 00:02:29,733
My doctoral dissertation.

57
00:02:29,733 --> 00:02:30,901
It's here.

58
00:02:30,901 --> 00:02:32,319
Yeah, it's right down here

59
00:02:32,319 --> 00:02:34,404
in the biggest library
in the university.

60
00:02:34,404 --> 00:02:35,489
Wow, that's actually
pretty cool.

61
00:02:35,489 --> 00:02:37,198
Yeah. Oh, um...

62
00:02:37,198 --> 00:02:41,369
There's also a book here by
a woman named Wendy Bagina.

63
00:02:42,955 --> 00:02:45,206
( ecstatic moaning )

64
00:02:45,206 --> 00:02:47,042
What is that?

65
00:02:47,042 --> 00:02:48,502
Sounds like two people

66
00:02:48,502 --> 00:02:51,546
are really enjoying
the Dewey decimal system.

67
00:02:55,550 --> 00:02:57,052
We're so sorry.

68
00:02:57,052 --> 00:02:58,345
Excuse us.

69
00:03:01,682 --> 00:03:04,518
You didn't bring me here
to do that, did you?

70
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:12,526
She sent the chicken back again?

71
00:03:12,526 --> 00:03:14,862
She said it's too dry now,
and she wants to come back here

72
00:03:14,862 --> 00:03:16,822
and explain to
you exactly how
she wants it.

73
00:03:16,822 --> 00:03:20,075
Hmm... Well, fine, I'd like
to meet this chicken expert.

74
00:03:20,075 --> 00:03:21,535
Send the Colonel in.

75
00:03:25,789 --> 00:03:26,957
Oh...

76
00:03:26,957 --> 00:03:29,543
my... God!

77
00:03:32,295 --> 00:03:34,297
Lucky bastard!

78
00:03:34,297 --> 00:03:35,841
Janice!

79
00:03:35,841 --> 00:03:37,300
How are you...

80
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:40,888
Miss Hot Shot Chef
at the big, fancy restaurant

81
00:03:40,888 --> 00:03:42,931
with the best chicken ever?

82
00:03:42,931 --> 00:03:45,475
( laughs )

83
00:03:45,475 --> 00:03:47,061
I'm fine.

84
00:03:47,061 --> 00:03:49,563
Oh, what is that
on your finger?

85
00:03:49,563 --> 00:03:50,814
I'm blind.

86
00:03:50,814 --> 00:03:53,232
Oh, uh...

87
00:03:53,232 --> 00:03:56,277
So? Who's the lucky guy?

88
00:03:58,697 --> 00:04:01,491
Oh... my... God!

89
00:04:01,491 --> 00:04:04,745
I am so sorry, sweetie.

90
00:04:04,745 --> 00:04:06,413
Are you okay?

91
00:04:06,413 --> 00:04:10,209
You didn't tell her we're
getting married, did you?

92
00:04:10,209 --> 00:04:11,752
Well, she saw the ring.

93
00:04:11,752 --> 00:04:12,920
Did she freak out?

94
00:04:12,920 --> 00:04:14,546
Well, she was shocked
when I told her

95
00:04:14,546 --> 00:04:16,381
but, then again,
so were most people.

96
00:04:16,381 --> 00:04:18,092
Right.

97
00:04:18,092 --> 00:04:20,886
She actually has a boyfriend,
you know, herself.

98
00:04:20,886 --> 00:04:22,888
Name's Clark.

99
00:04:22,888 --> 00:04:25,974
Uh, she also kind of invited
herself to our wedding.

100
00:04:25,974 --> 00:04:29,144
Clark, too.

101
00:04:29,144 --> 00:04:30,896
You said no, right?

102
00:04:30,896 --> 00:04:33,398
Huh?

103
00:04:33,398 --> 00:04:37,111
You said no, right?

104
00:04:37,111 --> 00:04:38,403
Well, she cornered me, I mean...

105
00:04:38,403 --> 00:04:39,988
she asked me if the wedding
was in town.

106
00:04:39,988 --> 00:04:41,489
I mean, what was I
supposed to do?

107
00:04:41,489 --> 00:04:42,616
Lie.

108
00:04:43,784 --> 00:04:45,577
How hard is that?

109
00:04:45,577 --> 00:04:47,079
Your check's in the mail.

110
00:04:47,079 --> 00:04:48,997
Oh, your baby is so cute.

111
00:04:48,997 --> 00:04:53,085
I can't wait
to read your book, Ross.

112
00:04:54,962 --> 00:04:56,588
So she'll
come to the wedding.

113
00:04:56,588 --> 00:04:58,298
Maybe it won't be so bad.

114
00:04:58,298 --> 00:05:00,259
What, do you think she's just
going to sit there quietly?

115
00:05:00,259 --> 00:05:02,343
You don't think she's going
to want to make a toast?

116
00:05:02,343 --> 00:05:04,387
You don't think she's going to
want to grab the microphone

117
00:05:04,387 --> 00:05:06,140
and sing "Part-time Lover"?

118
00:05:06,140 --> 00:05:07,306
Oh, my God!

119
00:05:07,306 --> 00:05:08,642
She's not going to like
the chicken

120
00:05:08,642 --> 00:05:10,602
that night either,
is she?

121
00:05:13,855 --> 00:05:15,190
You know what?

122
00:05:15,190 --> 00:05:16,817
It's going to be okay.
You know what?

123
00:05:16,817 --> 00:05:18,777
She's probably not going
to even want to come.

124
00:05:18,777 --> 00:05:19,861
Really?

125
00:05:19,861 --> 00:05:22,363
No, that was a lie.

126
00:05:22,363 --> 00:05:24,574
See how easy that was?

127
00:05:24,574 --> 00:05:25,993
So, so...

128
00:05:25,993 --> 00:05:28,287
You would have just lied?

129
00:05:28,287 --> 00:05:30,038
Yes.

130
00:05:30,038 --> 00:05:31,748
It would have really
been that easy?

131
00:05:31,748 --> 00:05:33,875
Yes.

132
00:05:33,875 --> 00:05:35,460
Good, so do it
Saturday night

133
00:05:35,460 --> 00:05:37,462
'cause we're going to
dinner with her and Clark.

134
00:05:39,047 --> 00:05:41,800
( giggles )

135
00:05:44,303 --> 00:05:45,762
Hey, what's up?

136
00:05:45,762 --> 00:05:47,848
Hey!
Hey!

137
00:05:47,848 --> 00:05:49,348
Oh, hey, who's your friend?

138
00:05:50,433 --> 00:05:52,560
Hey!

139
00:05:52,560 --> 00:05:54,562
Hey, Joey.

140
00:05:54,562 --> 00:05:56,898
Erin, you're still here.

141
00:05:56,898 --> 00:05:59,901
Yeah, we ended up spending
the day together

142
00:05:59,901 --> 00:06:02,529
and had such a great time.

143
00:06:02,529 --> 00:06:03,947
Why wouldn't you?

144
00:06:03,947 --> 00:06:06,074
Erin is great.

145
00:06:06,074 --> 00:06:08,994
And then there's you guys.

146
00:06:08,994 --> 00:06:11,746
Well, listen, I'd
better get going.

147
00:06:11,746 --> 00:06:13,290
Today was great, thanks.

148
00:06:13,290 --> 00:06:14,624
I know.
Okay.

149
00:06:14,624 --> 00:06:16,210
And Joey...

150
00:06:16,210 --> 00:06:17,294
Last night was fun.

151
00:06:17,294 --> 00:06:18,337
Yeah.

152
00:06:18,337 --> 00:06:19,713
I'll, uh, I'll call you.

153
00:06:19,713 --> 00:06:20,797
Oh, and I'll call you, too.

154
00:06:20,797 --> 00:06:22,007
Or I'll call you.

155
00:06:22,007 --> 00:06:23,342
And call me.

156
00:06:23,342 --> 00:06:24,843
Okay.

157
00:06:24,843 --> 00:06:25,760
Okay, good to
see you again.

158
00:06:25,760 --> 00:06:27,054
Bye.
Bye-bye.

159
00:06:27,054 --> 00:06:29,472
Rachel:
Bye.

160
00:06:29,472 --> 00:06:32,934
So, system kind
of broke down, huh?

161
00:06:32,934 --> 00:06:33,977
Oh, Joey, I'm sorry.

162
00:06:33,977 --> 00:06:35,354
I just couldn't tell her

163
00:06:35,354 --> 00:06:37,022
all those things you
wanted me to tell her.

164
00:06:37,022 --> 00:06:39,566
And, you know, we
got to talking, and...

165
00:06:39,566 --> 00:06:41,526
We want you to marry her.

166
00:06:41,526 --> 00:06:43,611
What?

167
00:06:43,611 --> 00:06:46,240
She is so amazing,
you have no idea.

168
00:06:46,240 --> 00:06:48,407
No idea? Who do you
think brought her here?

169
00:06:48,407 --> 00:06:50,077
Cupid.

170
00:06:51,912 --> 00:06:53,163
Joey, she's so cool.

171
00:06:53,163 --> 00:06:54,622
She speaks four languages.

172
00:06:54,622 --> 00:06:57,792
Man, do you know
what guys want!

173
00:07:00,712 --> 00:07:01,755
No, Joey, come on.

174
00:07:01,755 --> 00:07:03,382
She's so perfect for you.

175
00:07:03,382 --> 00:07:05,884
I mean, she's sweet, she,
she likes baseball...

176
00:07:05,884 --> 00:07:07,969
and she, she had two beers
at lunch.

177
00:07:07,969 --> 00:07:09,637
My beers?

178
00:07:11,014 --> 00:07:12,933
Look, you guys, she's a very
nice girl, okay?

179
00:07:12,933 --> 00:07:14,433
We had a good time.

180
00:07:14,433 --> 00:07:16,353
But I just... I don't see it
going anywhere.

181
00:07:16,353 --> 00:07:17,896
Yeah, but you
always say that.

182
00:07:17,896 --> 00:07:19,940
Yeah, maybe if you gave
this girl a chance

183
00:07:19,940 --> 00:07:21,108
it would go somewhere.

184
00:07:21,108 --> 00:07:22,734
Look, I'm sorry, you guys.

185
00:07:22,734 --> 00:07:24,194
I just don't think so.

186
00:07:24,194 --> 00:07:25,362
Whatever.

187
00:07:25,362 --> 00:07:26,487
Fine.

188
00:07:26,487 --> 00:07:28,365
Hey, don't start judging me.

189
00:07:28,365 --> 00:07:31,743
Huh? You're the one who's
in love with her assistant, huh?

190
00:07:31,743 --> 00:07:33,912
And you, you're the one
who's having the affair

191
00:07:33,912 --> 00:07:35,830
with the guy who keeps
the pigeons on the roof.

192
00:07:35,830 --> 00:07:37,916
Phoebe!

193
00:07:37,916 --> 00:07:40,585
Secret affair.

194
00:07:49,803 --> 00:07:52,973
People are doing it
in front of my book.

195
00:07:52,973 --> 00:07:55,267
I'm sorry?

196
00:07:55,267 --> 00:07:58,937
My doctoral dissertation
is in the library at school.

197
00:07:58,937 --> 00:08:02,732
I went to see it, and there were
students making babies...

198
00:08:02,732 --> 00:08:06,069
right in the middle
of the paleontology section.

199
00:08:06,069 --> 00:08:09,739
Oh, my God! Did you get
to see anything good?

200
00:08:09,739 --> 00:08:11,366
Let me ask you something.

201
00:08:11,366 --> 00:08:14,702
At your school, was there, like,
a place on campus

202
00:08:14,702 --> 00:08:17,622
where students went to,
to fool around?

203
00:08:17,622 --> 00:08:19,333
Yeah, there was.

204
00:08:19,333 --> 00:08:23,211
In the corner of the library
where all these dusty books were

205
00:08:23,211 --> 00:08:25,922
that nobody ever read,
yes, there was.

206
00:08:25,922 --> 00:08:28,467
Great, 'cause people
kept showing up.

207
00:08:28,467 --> 00:08:30,427
I think it's like a thing.

208
00:08:30,427 --> 00:08:32,595
Wait, hold on a second.

209
00:08:32,595 --> 00:08:36,183
Fifth floor, against
that back wall?

210
00:08:36,183 --> 00:08:39,644
Oh, for crying out loud!

211
00:08:42,481 --> 00:08:44,524
All right, so we should
go catch our movie.

212
00:08:44,524 --> 00:08:46,360
Well, now, what's the rush?

213
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:48,278
I like to see the previews.

214
00:08:48,278 --> 00:08:50,989
The candy.

215
00:08:50,989 --> 00:08:54,075
Oh, hey.

216
00:08:54,075 --> 00:08:55,535
Well, look who's here.

217
00:08:55,535 --> 00:08:57,329
Hey, Joey.
Hey, Erin.

218
00:08:57,329 --> 00:08:59,247
Hey, Rachel.
Hi.

219
00:08:59,247 --> 00:09:01,458
Well, we were just
about to take off
and see a movie.

220
00:09:01,458 --> 00:09:02,750
Yeah.
Oh.

221
00:09:02,750 --> 00:09:03,918
Oh, no.

222
00:09:03,918 --> 00:09:05,420
What's wrong?

223
00:09:05,420 --> 00:09:09,757
Oh, Phoebe, we forgot
that party we have to go to.

224
00:09:09,757 --> 00:09:11,801
Oh, no.

225
00:09:11,801 --> 00:09:13,845
What party?

226
00:09:13,845 --> 00:09:16,681
A birthday party.

227
00:09:16,681 --> 00:09:18,433
Oh, whose birthday party?

228
00:09:18,433 --> 00:09:21,520
Both:
Allison's birthday party.

229
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:24,814
Oh? And how old is Allison?

230
00:09:24,814 --> 00:09:26,525
Both:
Thirty-two.

231
00:09:28,109 --> 00:09:29,694
Wait a minute...

232
00:09:29,694 --> 00:09:33,240
Why don't you
guys do something?

233
00:09:33,240 --> 00:09:36,368
Yeah, look how
that worked out.

234
00:09:40,288 --> 00:09:41,331
Excuse me?

235
00:09:41,331 --> 00:09:43,083
Hi. I'm a professor here.

236
00:09:43,083 --> 00:09:45,835
Do you know
the Paleontology section

237
00:09:45,835 --> 00:09:48,422
fifth floor, stack 437?

238
00:09:48,422 --> 00:09:50,465
Well, yes.

239
00:09:50,465 --> 00:09:51,841
Just give me five minutes.

240
00:09:51,841 --> 00:09:54,177
I just have to find someone
to cover my shift.

241
00:09:55,678 --> 00:09:59,349
No, no, no.

242
00:09:59,349 --> 00:10:02,561
Can I speak to someone
in charge, please?

243
00:10:06,231 --> 00:10:07,941
How can I help you?

244
00:10:07,941 --> 00:10:10,193
Hi. I was wondering,
is it possible

245
00:10:10,193 --> 00:10:11,319
to increase security

246
00:10:11,319 --> 00:10:13,280
in the Paleontology section?

247
00:10:13,280 --> 00:10:15,323
See, I-I wrote a book
that's up there

248
00:10:15,323 --> 00:10:17,867
and instead of reading it,
people are-are...

249
00:10:17,867 --> 00:10:20,995
well, they're rolling around
in front of it.

250
00:10:20,995 --> 00:10:24,749
We are aware of the problem
you're referring to.

251
00:10:29,254 --> 00:10:31,005
But as far as increasing

252
00:10:31,005 --> 00:10:34,175
security, I'm afraid the library
is very understaffed.

253
00:10:34,175 --> 00:10:36,636
I-I can't help you.

254
00:10:36,636 --> 00:10:38,637
Well, fine. Fine.

255
00:10:38,637 --> 00:10:40,181
If-if I'm the only person

256
00:10:40,181 --> 00:10:41,975
with, uh, any
appreciation
of the sanctity

257
00:10:41,975 --> 00:10:43,893
of the written word,
then I'll go up there

258
00:10:43,893 --> 00:10:46,187
and defend it myself.

259
00:10:46,187 --> 00:10:48,273
And don't you follow me.

260
00:10:50,275 --> 00:10:51,485
Hey.

261
00:10:51,485 --> 00:10:52,693
Oh, hey.
Hey.

262
00:10:52,693 --> 00:10:54,112
How did it go with Erin?

263
00:10:54,112 --> 00:10:55,905
Oh, unbelievable.

264
00:10:55,905 --> 00:10:58,158
We had the best time.

265
00:10:58,158 --> 00:10:59,409
Yeah!
Yeah!

266
00:10:59,409 --> 00:11:01,244
Oh, so you're not
mad at us anymore?

267
00:11:01,244 --> 00:11:03,037
No. no. no.
You guys were totally right.

268
00:11:03,037 --> 00:11:05,332
This was so much better
than the first time we went out.

269
00:11:05,332 --> 00:11:06,583
That was so awkward.

270
00:11:06,583 --> 00:11:08,251
We were both really nervous.

271
00:11:08,251 --> 00:11:09,628
Didn't you sleep together?

272
00:11:09,628 --> 00:11:11,588
Yeah. That really calms me down.

273
00:11:13,423 --> 00:11:16,468
And... we have so much
in common.

274
00:11:16,468 --> 00:11:18,178
She-she loves sandwiches.

275
00:11:18,178 --> 00:11:21,515
Sports... although,
she is a Met fan.

276
00:11:21,515 --> 00:11:24,643
Not much of an issue now,
but if were ever to have kids...

277
00:11:24,643 --> 00:11:26,019
Oh, my God!

278
00:11:26,019 --> 00:11:28,271
Listen to you
talking about
having kids.

279
00:11:28,271 --> 00:11:29,397
Oh.

280
00:11:29,397 --> 00:11:30,607
Oh, my Joey.

281
00:11:30,607 --> 00:11:31,899
Oh!

282
00:11:31,899 --> 00:11:33,360
Please don't get married
before I do.

283
00:11:33,360 --> 00:11:34,361
Oh.

284
00:11:34,361 --> 00:11:35,445
Okay?

285
00:11:38,948 --> 00:11:41,034
Oh. I just

286
00:11:41,034 --> 00:11:44,287
cannot believe that Clark
stood me up.

287
00:11:44,287 --> 00:11:45,955
He may still show up.

288
00:11:45,955 --> 00:11:47,499
Oh, what are you, stupid?

289
00:11:48,583 --> 00:11:50,335
It's been three hours!

290
00:11:50,335 --> 00:11:52,837
Is that all?

291
00:11:52,837 --> 00:11:55,756
Let's just go on
to happier things, okay?

292
00:11:55,756 --> 00:11:59,553
Um, why don't you tell me
about your lovely wedding?

293
00:11:59,553 --> 00:12:01,304
Well, actually, uh,
there was something

294
00:12:01,304 --> 00:12:03,306
that we wanted to tell you
about the wedding, um...

295
00:12:03,306 --> 00:12:04,723
( clears throat )

296
00:12:04,723 --> 00:12:07,810
It's going to be
a-a small ceremony.

297
00:12:07,810 --> 00:12:09,187
Uh, tiny.

298
00:12:09,187 --> 00:12:13,732
We're not even sure
why we're having it.

299
00:12:13,732 --> 00:12:17,820
It's actually going
to be just family.

300
00:12:17,820 --> 00:12:22,033
Oh... wait.

301
00:12:23,493 --> 00:12:26,413
You two think of me as family?

302
00:12:28,747 --> 00:12:33,044
Oh, I have to ask you
something now, and be honest.

303
00:12:33,044 --> 00:12:35,213
Do you want me to sing

304
00:12:35,213 --> 00:12:38,216
"Careless Whisper"
or "Lady in Red"?

305
00:12:41,428 --> 00:12:42,470
How can you say that?

306
00:12:42,470 --> 00:12:44,055
The Mets have no closer.

307
00:12:44,055 --> 00:12:45,181
What about Benitez?

308
00:12:45,181 --> 00:12:47,601
What about game one
of the series?

309
00:12:47,601 --> 00:12:48,643
What about, shut up?

310
00:12:48,643 --> 00:12:50,019
You shut up.

311
00:12:50,019 --> 00:12:52,313
I love arguing with her.

312
00:12:52,313 --> 00:12:53,772
I'll be right back.

313
00:12:53,772 --> 00:12:56,484
Okay.

314
00:12:56,484 --> 00:12:58,027
So, how's it going
with Joey?

315
00:12:58,027 --> 00:13:00,238
Uh... okay.

316
00:13:00,238 --> 00:13:01,322
Okay?

317
00:13:01,322 --> 00:13:02,865
Wait, okay.

318
00:13:02,865 --> 00:13:04,451
Tell me
that you like him, please?

319
00:13:04,451 --> 00:13:05,952
I mean, tell me
that you like him.

320
00:13:05,952 --> 00:13:08,288
Look, he's a really great guy,
and I know

321
00:13:08,288 --> 00:13:10,789
that you really want this
to work out

322
00:13:10,789 --> 00:13:13,876
but... I just don't see
this having a future.

323
00:13:13,876 --> 00:13:15,629
What?

324
00:13:15,629 --> 00:13:18,214
But you said
that you liked him.

325
00:13:18,214 --> 00:13:19,466
I mean, what happened?

326
00:13:19,466 --> 00:13:22,302
Did you just
change your mind?

327
00:13:22,302 --> 00:13:23,428
Kind of.

328
00:13:23,428 --> 00:13:25,430
Then change it back!

329
00:13:25,430 --> 00:13:27,432
I'm sorry.

330
00:13:27,432 --> 00:13:30,226
I... it's just,
there's no real spark.

331
00:13:30,226 --> 00:13:32,353
No spark?
Didn't you sleep together?

332
00:13:32,353 --> 00:13:34,021
Yeah.

333
00:13:34,021 --> 00:13:35,523
Uh, tramp!

334
00:13:37,108 --> 00:13:39,402
Does Joey have any idea?

335
00:13:39,402 --> 00:13:40,570
I really don't
think he does.

336
00:13:40,570 --> 00:13:41,862
And you know what?

337
00:13:41,862 --> 00:13:43,323
Maybe you guys
could help clue him in.

338
00:13:43,323 --> 00:13:44,949
You know, tell him
I'm not interested

339
00:13:44,949 --> 00:13:46,951
in a serious relationship
or something.

340
00:13:46,951 --> 00:13:50,747
Yeah. You mean, like, that
you're kind of a loner?

341
00:13:50,747 --> 00:13:52,206
Yeah. That'd be great.

342
00:13:52,206 --> 00:13:55,335
Yeah, and maybe that
you're a real stronzo.

343
00:13:55,335 --> 00:13:56,377
I'm sorry?

344
00:13:56,377 --> 00:13:57,754
Well, I guess Italian

345
00:13:57,754 --> 00:14:00,340
isn't one of the four
languages you speak.

346
00:14:02,049 --> 00:14:04,385
Hey... want to go?

347
00:14:04,385 --> 00:14:05,428
Yeah, let's go.

348
00:14:05,428 --> 00:14:06,887
Okay. See you guys later.

349
00:14:06,887 --> 00:14:08,515
Bye, guys.
See ya.

350
00:14:09,766 --> 00:14:11,810
Hey, thank you so much.

351
00:14:14,521 --> 00:14:16,731
Wow!

352
00:14:16,731 --> 00:14:19,025
Well, I guess it wasn't Cupid
that brought her here.

353
00:14:19,025 --> 00:14:23,070
No. Just regular
old flying dwarf.

354
00:14:29,994 --> 00:14:31,329
Yes? Yes?

355
00:14:31,329 --> 00:14:32,913
How can I help you?

356
00:14:32,913 --> 00:14:34,791
Uh, we were just
looking around.

357
00:14:34,791 --> 00:14:37,335
Oh. Oh. You're-you're
fellow scholars.

358
00:14:37,335 --> 00:14:40,171
What exactly were
you looking for? Hmm?

359
00:14:40,171 --> 00:14:41,464
Perhaps, uh...

360
00:14:41,464 --> 00:14:44,300
Perhaps... Dr. Chester
Stock's musings

361
00:14:44,300 --> 00:14:46,594
on the Smilodon
Californicus?

362
00:14:48,137 --> 00:14:49,556
Uh...

363
00:14:49,556 --> 00:14:51,432
"Uh, uh..."
Get out of here!

364
00:15:00,483 --> 00:15:02,485
Hi. Meeting someone?

365
00:15:02,485 --> 00:15:05,530
Or-or are you just
here to brush up

366
00:15:05,530 --> 00:15:08,616
on Merriam's views
on evolution?

367
00:15:08,616 --> 00:15:13,621
Actually, I find Merriam's views
far too progressionist.

368
00:15:17,709 --> 00:15:21,128
I find Merriam's views
far too progressionist.

369
00:15:22,046 --> 00:15:23,381
I'm sorry.

370
00:15:23,381 --> 00:15:24,841
Who are you?

371
00:15:24,841 --> 00:15:26,342
I'm a professor here.

372
00:15:26,342 --> 00:15:27,385
Uh, Ross Geller.

373
00:15:27,385 --> 00:15:28,595
Ross Geller?

374
00:15:28,595 --> 00:15:29,804
Why do I know that name?

375
00:15:29,804 --> 00:15:32,348
It's a... wait.

376
00:15:35,685 --> 00:15:37,937
Did you write this?

377
00:15:37,937 --> 00:15:40,398
Yes.

378
00:15:42,817 --> 00:15:47,363
You're the person
who checked out my book?

379
00:15:47,363 --> 00:15:52,326
You know, you look nothing
like I would have thought.

380
00:15:52,326 --> 00:15:55,162
You're-you're so young.

381
00:15:55,162 --> 00:15:59,125
Well, I, uh... I
skipped fourth grade.

382
00:15:59,125 --> 00:16:00,334
Uh-huh.

383
00:16:07,634 --> 00:16:11,512
I am very, very sorry.

384
00:16:17,393 --> 00:16:19,103
Hey.

385
00:16:19,103 --> 00:16:20,271
Hey.

386
00:16:20,271 --> 00:16:21,188
Hi.

387
00:16:21,188 --> 00:16:22,398
So how was
your date?

388
00:16:22,398 --> 00:16:23,357
Oh, it was great.

389
00:16:23,357 --> 00:16:24,400
I mean, we walked

390
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:25,610
all around the village.

391
00:16:25,610 --> 00:16:26,820
We-we went to
this ice cream place

392
00:16:26,820 --> 00:16:27,862
split a milk shake.

393
00:16:27,862 --> 00:16:29,906
70-30, but still.

394
00:16:29,906 --> 00:16:31,616
And guess what?

395
00:16:31,616 --> 00:16:33,117
I'm thinking of
taking her upstate

396
00:16:33,117 --> 00:16:34,661
to one of those
bed and breakfasts.

397
00:16:34,661 --> 00:16:36,036
She said she wants
to go away with you?

398
00:16:36,036 --> 00:16:37,580
No, no, no, no, no.

399
00:16:37,580 --> 00:16:39,499
It's a surprise,
but it's going to be tricky

400
00:16:39,499 --> 00:16:42,084
because she's going to be
pretty busy at work for a while.

401
00:16:42,084 --> 00:16:44,211
Oh, yeah.

402
00:16:44,211 --> 00:16:47,507
Hey, Joey-Joey, look, honey,
we-we need to talk, okay?

403
00:16:47,507 --> 00:16:49,634
Um...

404
00:16:49,634 --> 00:16:51,928
I kind of got the feeling
from her today

405
00:16:51,928 --> 00:16:53,429
that, uh...

406
00:16:53,429 --> 00:16:56,432
that she's not looking
for a serious relationship.

407
00:16:56,432 --> 00:16:58,893
Where are you
getting this?

408
00:16:58,893 --> 00:17:00,269
Well, she told me.

409
00:17:01,980 --> 00:17:04,774
She said she's kind of a loner.

410
00:17:04,774 --> 00:17:06,860
Oh.

411
00:17:10,029 --> 00:17:12,072
Oh.

412
00:17:12,072 --> 00:17:13,407
Joey...

413
00:17:13,407 --> 00:17:15,869
Hey, Rach, it's
cool, you know?

414
00:17:15,869 --> 00:17:17,537
I'm a loner, too, right?

415
00:17:18,872 --> 00:17:20,456
Hey, Joey.

416
00:17:20,456 --> 00:17:22,500
You know what?
You are way
too good for her.

417
00:17:22,500 --> 00:17:25,169
Yeah, and I promise,
next time I will
just say good-bye

418
00:17:25,169 --> 00:17:27,755
and tell them you are not 
looking for a relationship.

419
00:17:27,755 --> 00:17:29,757
No.

420
00:17:29,757 --> 00:17:32,719
No. Don't do that.

421
00:17:32,719 --> 00:17:33,970
Just...

422
00:17:33,970 --> 00:17:36,890
Next time, make sure
she really likes me.

423
00:17:36,890 --> 00:17:38,808
Well, that, too.

424
00:17:42,311 --> 00:17:44,313
Joey?

425
00:17:46,024 --> 00:17:47,734
Yeah.

426
00:17:47,734 --> 00:17:49,443
Do you want
some pancakes?

427
00:17:49,443 --> 00:17:50,486
Finally.

428
00:17:50,486 --> 00:17:52,196
Okay.

429
00:17:53,489 --> 00:17:56,034
What are we going to do?

430
00:17:56,034 --> 00:17:58,411
I say we go with
"Careless Whisper."

431
00:17:59,787 --> 00:18:01,664
( knocking )

432
00:18:01,664 --> 00:18:03,416
Chandler?

433
00:18:03,416 --> 00:18:05,459
Did she see us yet?
Did she see us?

434
00:18:10,757 --> 00:18:13,051
Janice, what are you
doing here?

435
00:18:13,051 --> 00:18:14,552
Well, um...

436
00:18:14,552 --> 00:18:17,096
I thought I was going
to go back to my apartment

437
00:18:17,096 --> 00:18:18,514
but then I just felt like

438
00:18:18,514 --> 00:18:20,808
I really couldn't be alone
tonight.

439
00:18:26,940 --> 00:18:31,235
I was just wondering if I could
maybe stay here with you.

440
00:18:31,235 --> 00:18:34,447
Just, I really feel like I need
to be with family.

441
00:18:36,115 --> 00:18:38,952
Our kids are going to call her
Aunt Janice, aren't they?

442
00:18:38,952 --> 00:18:40,745
Please?

443
00:18:40,745 --> 00:18:45,124
It's just otherwise, I really
don't know what I might do.

444
00:18:45,124 --> 00:18:49,629
Aren't you just a
teensy bit curious?

445
00:18:49,629 --> 00:18:51,756
Ah! Do you have any tissues?

446
00:18:51,756 --> 00:18:52,882
In the bathroom.

447
00:18:52,882 --> 00:18:53,967
Okay.

448
00:18:56,886 --> 00:18:58,888
Just... just let her stay.

449
00:18:58,888 --> 00:19:00,139
No, no, no, no, no.

450
00:19:00,139 --> 00:19:03,476
If we let her stay,
she will stay forever.

451
00:19:03,476 --> 00:19:05,895
Kind of like your
Barcalounger.

452
00:19:05,895 --> 00:19:07,563
Is that what you're
thinking of right now?

453
00:19:07,563 --> 00:19:09,774
I never stop
thinking about it.

454
00:19:10,984 --> 00:19:12,860
Hey, you guys?

455
00:19:12,860 --> 00:19:14,779
Do either one of you
want to get in there

456
00:19:14,779 --> 00:19:16,238
before I take my bath?

457
00:19:18,324 --> 00:19:20,994
Janice, I'm sorry, but, uh...

458
00:19:20,994 --> 00:19:22,202
( clears throat )

459
00:19:22,202 --> 00:19:24,080
you can't stay here tonight.

460
00:19:24,080 --> 00:19:25,706
Why not?

461
00:19:25,706 --> 00:19:27,249
Honestly?

462
00:19:27,249 --> 00:19:30,210
Our apartment is a hotbed

463
00:19:30,210 --> 00:19:33,756
for electromagnetic activity.

464
00:19:35,257 --> 00:19:37,343
Now, Monica and I
have been immunized

465
00:19:37,343 --> 00:19:42,723
but, sadly, you have not.

466
00:19:42,723 --> 00:19:47,394
( guffawing )

467
00:19:47,394 --> 00:19:49,355
Okay, I'm going
to need a comforter

468
00:19:49,355 --> 00:19:51,398
but do you have
a hypo-allergenic one?

469
00:19:51,398 --> 00:19:53,484
Because otherwise
I get very nasal.

470
00:19:55,903 --> 00:19:57,697
( honks )
Do you have a cat?

471
00:19:57,697 --> 00:20:00,240
( honks )
'Cause it's already
happening.

472
00:20:00,240 --> 00:20:01,701
( honks )
You hear that? Listen.

473
00:20:01,701 --> 00:20:03,202
( honking )

474
00:20:03,202 --> 00:20:05,163
( honking angrily )

475
00:20:06,080 --> 00:20:07,832
Oh, my God!
Oh, my God!

476
00:20:07,832 --> 00:20:09,167
You have to go!

477
00:20:09,167 --> 00:20:10,417
Why?

478
00:20:12,837 --> 00:20:15,756
Because Chandler
still has feelings for you.

479
00:20:18,676 --> 00:20:20,469
He does?!

480
00:20:20,469 --> 00:20:22,513
Say again?

481
00:20:22,513 --> 00:20:25,474
That's right.
That's right.

482
00:20:25,474 --> 00:20:28,561
And that is why you
can't stay here tonight

483
00:20:28,561 --> 00:20:32,314
and probably why you shouldn't
come to the wedding.

484
00:20:32,314 --> 00:20:36,527
Feelings.
Such strong feelings.

485
00:20:36,527 --> 00:20:38,320
I mean...

486
00:20:38,320 --> 00:20:42,533
I realize that his
feelings may never
completely go away...

487
00:20:42,533 --> 00:20:44,827
but you can.

488
00:20:44,827 --> 00:20:48,372
Oh... my God.

489
00:20:48,372 --> 00:20:50,332
I understand.

490
00:20:50,332 --> 00:20:52,626
I'm so sorry.

491
00:20:52,626 --> 00:20:54,712
I'll go.

492
00:20:59,217 --> 00:21:01,135
Good-bye, Monica.

493
00:21:01,135 --> 00:21:04,138
I wish you a lifetime
of happiness with him.

494
00:21:05,556 --> 00:21:06,724
Chandler...

495
00:21:08,475 --> 00:21:11,020
You call me when this
goes in the pooper.

496
00:21:22,656 --> 00:21:24,491
Don't sweat it.

497
00:21:24,491 --> 00:21:25,993
I got this
section covered.

498
00:21:25,993 --> 00:21:28,079
Yeah, in fact, I got
this little baby

499
00:21:28,079 --> 00:21:31,040
to shine in people's eye...
okay, see you later.

500
00:21:40,091 --> 00:21:42,260
I just wanted to show
Monica your book.

